<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! sense.kapae.restores ~ the muted branch's entries reappear in recall

Restores a branch a mute set aside, across a sensorium: the rows never left (move-not-delete), so the restore finds each entry again and the entries reappear in recall. `sensorium` names it; absent, memory.

The answer is {branch, restored_entries, resolved}; a branch no turn names answers `resolved: false` with nothing restored. The terminal's `lares sense worldline un-kapae <branch>` names the same act and joins this address as a cli skin when the sense door flips.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/shows`>>

!! shows ~ a-branch

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`example` name=`a-branch` params=`branch/<branch> tick/1 ~ restore one branch at a tick`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/takes`>>

!! takes ~ branch · tick · sensorium

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`arg` name=`branch` params=`takes/branch-root needs/required ~ the muted branch to restore, by the root turn-key of its fork`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`tick` params=`takes/whole-number needs/required ~ the tick the restore lands at`>>
<<has entity=`arg` name=`sensorium` params=`takes/name ~ the sensorium to restore across; absent, memory`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/gate`>>

!! gate ~ write

Testimony: the door checks; this slot grants nothing.

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`gate` name=`write` params=`who/seat-or-hand ~ reversible and trusted: a restore the seat runs on the operator's loop`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/answers`>>

!! answers ~ restored · unresolved

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`band` name=`restored` params=`exit/0 fields/[[branch restored_entries resolved]] ~ the branch's entries reappear in recall`>>
<<has entity=`band` name=`unresolved` params=`exit/0 ~ the branch names no turn; resolved reads false and nothing restored`>>
```

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins`>>

!! skins ~ mcp

<<~ ahu slot=`#/skins/mcp`>>

!!! un_kapae

```memetic-wikitext
<<has entity=`skin` name=`mcp` params=`handler/host spells/un_kapae ~ the seat`>>
```

